WEBVTT

00:01.530 --> 00:04.670
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.670 --> 00:08.200
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.200 --> 00:16.130
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.320 --> 00:27.960
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.960 --> 00:33.860
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.860 --> 00:42.800
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.800 --> 00:47.510
Like the wind

00:47.510 --> 00:50.580
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.580 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.660
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.660 --> 01:07.400
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.400 --> 01:13.540
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.540 --> 01:20.210
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.210 --> 01:27.510
The roadless journey continues

01:37.860 --> 01:39.860
No way!

01:39.860 --> 01:42.590
The coin's answer is the same.

01:49.600 --> 01:52.540
Do we absolutely have to
take the road in that direction?

01:52.540 --> 01:53.880
Yes.

01:53.880 --> 01:55.380
Why is that?

01:55.380 --> 01:57.250
I don't know.

01:57.250 --> 02:01.220
Talking to you, I feel like my
brain's going to turn into tacos.

02:01.220 --> 02:04.220
♪ Taco, taco, tacos! Tasty... ♪

02:04.220 --> 02:06.550
You don't have to sing.

02:06.550 --> 02:10.820
♪... tacos! The most awesome tacos are... ♪

02:17.570 --> 02:21.930
The two were continuing their journey,
just as they had been doing.

02:27.110 --> 02:29.440
It's shining...

02:29.440 --> 02:33.970
However, a small change
was beginning to take place.

02:37.920 --> 02:42.490
Through Blue-eyes' efforts,
we now know the full extent

02:42.490 --> 02:47.190
of Douglas Rosenberg's Project Leviathan.

02:53.430 --> 02:56.640
It is dangerous to leave Ellis at large.

02:56.640 --> 02:59.010
We should dispose of her at once.

02:59.010 --> 03:03.010
However, they are acting on the assumption

03:03.010 --> 03:05.510
that we have obtained this information.

03:05.510 --> 03:10.720
If we act hastily, they may
use that to their advantage.

03:10.720 --> 03:15.490
Unless we devise a plan, we are
merely asking for the worst to happen.

03:15.490 --> 03:18.890
I believe I answered that question before.

03:18.890 --> 03:22.000
I have no need to know just who Ellis is.

03:22.000 --> 03:25.700
I just have to protect her until
I have further instructions.

03:25.700 --> 03:27.200
That's what you're going to say, right?

03:27.200 --> 03:31.310
Like a machine talking, with zero emotion.

03:31.310 --> 03:34.180
The last part was unnecessary,
but that's exactly right.

03:34.180 --> 03:36.380
But I'm not satisfied.

03:36.380 --> 03:38.250
- ls it necessary?
- What?

03:38.250 --> 03:41.150
If you remain in the dark
about just who Ellis is,

03:41.150 --> 03:42.980
will that hinder you in your work?

03:42.980 --> 03:44.550
That's...

03:44.550 --> 03:46.820
At any rate, make your
mission your top priority.

03:46.820 --> 03:49.480
- Understood?
- Oh, w-wait, hold on...

03:57.570 --> 03:59.900
Ooh, that ticks me off! I swear!

03:59.900 --> 04:03.500
So you two are headed south?

04:03.500 --> 04:07.410
A word of friendly advice. You should
go back the way you came right away.

04:07.410 --> 04:08.780
Why?

04:08.780 --> 04:13.550
There's a village up ahead,
but the folks living there are a little...

04:13.550 --> 04:16.720
If we're talking bounty hunters and scoundrels,

04:16.720 --> 04:18.290
I don't have any problems with that.

04:18.290 --> 04:21.190
Because Nadie's a scoundrel, too.

04:21.190 --> 04:22.520
Hey.

04:22.520 --> 04:24.630
Anyway, if you want to go south,

04:24.630 --> 04:27.230
you should go back and go through the town.

04:27.230 --> 04:31.030
I mean, it'll make for a lengthy
detour, but better that than...

04:31.030 --> 04:33.870
We can't. We're going straight.

04:33.870 --> 04:35.770
Why, of all things...

04:35.770 --> 04:37.870
Please don't ask why.

04:37.870 --> 04:40.810
If you ask, your brain will turn into tacos.

04:46.480 --> 04:48.280
What's that?

04:52.050 --> 04:54.390
Ellis, be careful.

04:54.390 --> 04:56.080
Yessir.

04:57.260 --> 04:58.730
Where are you headed?

04:58.730 --> 05:00.960
Do you have some business in our village?

05:00.960 --> 05:02.400
No business.

05:02.400 --> 05:04.490
We're just passing through.

05:06.830 --> 05:08.070
Very well.

05:08.070 --> 05:12.240
But right now, our village is in
the midst of a sacred festival.

05:12.240 --> 05:15.680
If you're going to pass through,
you'll have to do as we say.

05:17.750 --> 05:19.950
Huh?

05:19.950 --> 05:21.480
Choose one.

05:21.480 --> 05:23.480
Choose?

05:23.480 --> 05:25.350
We have to wear them, too?

05:25.350 --> 05:28.590
That is what our custom dictates.

05:28.590 --> 05:31.750
- It's heavy.
- It stinks.

05:39.170 --> 05:41.300
It doesn't look right on you.

05:41.300 --> 05:43.330
Same to you, too.

05:47.440 --> 05:49.770
They're all dressed the same.

05:52.110 --> 05:54.670
Probably another part of their so-called custom.

05:55.980 --> 06:00.790
- Guardian Goddess Chappy!
- Guardian Goddess Chappy!

06:00.790 --> 06:09.660
- Please bless us with wealth and good fortune!
- Please bless us with wealth and good fortune!

06:09.660 --> 06:14.070
- Goddess Chappy!
- Goddess Chappy!

06:14.070 --> 06:16.340
Don't parrot their words for no reason.

06:16.340 --> 06:17.970
Cute, isn't it?

06:17.970 --> 06:19.840
You've got to be kidding me.

06:19.840 --> 06:21.970
Wait... Ellis?

06:24.350 --> 06:26.150
Cute...

06:26.150 --> 06:27.980
It's Lady Natalya!

06:38.360 --> 06:41.590
I feel like I've seen her somewhere...

06:50.870 --> 06:53.270
Behold my witch's powers!

06:59.210 --> 07:01.720
Everyone, don't be fooled!

07:01.720 --> 07:03.920
Miracles like that are fake!

07:03.920 --> 07:08.360
Foolish youth, you had
better watch your tongues.

07:08.360 --> 07:09.920
Shut up, you charlatan!

07:09.920 --> 07:12.230
Give back the money you fleeced from us!

07:12.230 --> 07:14.090
I remember now!

07:27.110 --> 07:29.810
Behold! That girl is another of my kind,

07:29.810 --> 07:33.870
whom I have summoned with my witch's powers.

07:36.280 --> 07:38.050
Ellis!

08:14.460 --> 08:16.590
Where are we?

08:16.590 --> 08:19.160
How much do you remember
of what happened earlier?

08:19.160 --> 08:22.530
Up to where the weird woman showed up...

08:22.530 --> 08:26.530
We're at that weird woman's house.

08:26.530 --> 08:28.970
Welcome to the witch's manor house.

08:28.970 --> 08:31.870
Well, well, we appreciate the formal welcome.

08:31.870 --> 08:34.010
You seem to be non-believers.

08:34.010 --> 08:38.510
However, you are travelers. I shall forgive you.

08:38.510 --> 08:40.380
I was originally...

08:42.220 --> 08:44.120
Wait, you can't touch that...

08:48.820 --> 08:51.460
You can drop the act already.

08:51.460 --> 08:53.490
I know.

08:53.490 --> 08:55.530
What?

08:55.530 --> 08:59.730
You're the psychic girl who had
the world buzzing a long time ago.

08:59.730 --> 09:01.900
Nastarsha, right?

09:06.810 --> 09:11.010
Oh, if you knew, then I
wish you'd said so first.

09:15.820 --> 09:17.650
Cute.

09:17.650 --> 09:19.490
Her name's Chappy.

09:19.490 --> 09:23.080
She died last year, though. Of diabetes.

09:24.860 --> 09:30.160
Your pet had diabetes?
What kind of life do you lead?

09:30.160 --> 09:32.930
What's wrong with living extravagantly?

09:32.930 --> 09:35.570
I've got more money than I could ever spend.

09:35.570 --> 09:39.410
You fleeced the villagers
of that money anyway, right?

09:39.410 --> 09:42.410
Would you please not make it
sound like I did something bad?

09:42.410 --> 09:44.570
They were donations given out of good will.

09:45.680 --> 09:47.840
Those are of when I was little.

09:49.080 --> 09:52.920
America, Britain, Japan, China...

09:52.920 --> 09:56.760
That was when I was really
raking it in all over the world.

09:56.760 --> 10:00.450
I even had a palatial
mansion built in Beverly Hills.

10:06.300 --> 10:10.640
But they found out that I'd been faking it.

10:10.640 --> 10:13.210
And then it was just a huge mess.

10:13.210 --> 10:15.880
The entire world was clamoring about it.

10:15.880 --> 10:18.150
Well, of course, they would.

10:18.150 --> 10:21.120
In the end, I lost absolutely everything.

10:21.120 --> 10:23.780
I came here after wandering all over the place

10:23.780 --> 10:27.720
and found what they call a
fateful encounter waiting for me.

10:27.720 --> 10:33.730
This region has a ton of old
legends concerning witches.

10:33.730 --> 10:37.060
I just knew that I could use that!

10:40.740 --> 10:45.840
The Council is leaning towards a
decision that is undesirable for us.

10:45.840 --> 10:49.780
Then, they intend to
allow Ellis to remain alive?

10:49.780 --> 10:53.110
She was originally created at the hands of man.

10:53.110 --> 10:55.520
If a creature born out of
nothing is allowed to live,

10:55.520 --> 10:58.090
she will surely prove to
be the seed of disaster.

10:58.090 --> 10:59.950
I agree.

10:59.950 --> 11:02.420
In the worst case scenario,

11:02.420 --> 11:07.120
we may ignore their decision
and invoke the Law of the Night.

11:09.160 --> 11:12.930
Preparations have already been made.

11:24.810 --> 11:26.550
Please believe me!

11:26.550 --> 11:29.450
I am a real psychic!

11:29.450 --> 11:32.290
- That's enough already!
- Tell us the truth!

11:32.290 --> 11:35.120
I've told you over and over again, haven't I?

11:35.120 --> 11:40.190
I will admit that I lied, but I am a real...

11:45.630 --> 11:47.130
Don't come over here!

11:47.130 --> 11:50.400
Go away, witch!

11:50.400 --> 11:52.640
I...

11:52.640 --> 11:56.840
I'm no... witch...

12:14.830 --> 12:16.690
Just a little, all right?

12:18.500 --> 12:20.090
Meow...

12:36.850 --> 12:38.580
Can't sleep?

12:40.220 --> 12:42.760
No.

12:42.760 --> 12:45.230
Why don't you go out for a walk or something?

12:45.230 --> 12:47.060
I think I will.

12:59.040 --> 13:02.880
Say, were you bullied when you were little, too?

13:02.880 --> 13:04.380
Why?

13:04.380 --> 13:08.440
You also have powers that
normal humans don't have, right?

13:11.890 --> 13:14.760
I was bullied.

13:14.760 --> 13:17.320
They called me witch and stuff.

13:17.320 --> 13:19.320
Even though you're a fake?

13:24.630 --> 13:27.660
- That tickles.
- Stay still.

13:32.910 --> 13:34.240
I can feel it...

13:34.240 --> 13:38.080
♪ Taco, taco, tacos! Tasty tacos! ♪

13:38.080 --> 13:40.410
That's really become a
favorite of yours, hasn't it?

13:40.410 --> 13:42.640
You wouldn't sing it, Nadie?

13:45.150 --> 13:47.350
"You wouldn't sing it, Nadie?"

13:49.420 --> 13:50.960
Do you get it now?

13:50.960 --> 13:55.200
I can read people's memories.

13:55.200 --> 13:58.470
This power alone is real.

13:58.470 --> 14:01.540
Everyone, we've found out
that woman's true identity!

14:01.540 --> 14:07.980
Long ago, she got the world in an
uproar over her fake psychic powers!

14:07.980 --> 14:10.710
We've been deceived!

14:10.710 --> 14:12.380
Wake up!

14:12.380 --> 14:15.140
The Goddess Chappy is just some trickery!

14:22.720 --> 14:24.710
This guy...

14:26.130 --> 14:27.960
From that one time...

14:35.000 --> 14:36.640
Are you all right?

14:36.640 --> 14:39.470
Not him, I guess.

14:46.980 --> 14:49.850
Are you happy?

14:49.850 --> 14:54.220
Nothing good ever happened to me.

14:54.220 --> 14:57.560
Sure, I never had to worry about money,

14:57.560 --> 15:00.900
but both my mom and dad relied on my income,

15:00.900 --> 15:03.560
and they were always fighting.

15:03.560 --> 15:05.570
And the moment people found out I was fake,

15:05.570 --> 15:08.840
they both grabbed the money and ran.

15:08.840 --> 15:10.670
If I didn't have any psychic powers,

15:10.670 --> 15:12.870
I could've been normal and gone to school,

15:12.870 --> 15:15.040
goofed around with friends,

15:15.040 --> 15:18.210
found a boyfriend, got married...

15:18.210 --> 15:22.050
I think I would've had
a proper life like that...

15:22.050 --> 15:24.390
Wait... Hey, what are you doing?!

15:24.390 --> 15:26.590
That's Chappy's!

15:26.590 --> 15:27.890
Just a little taste.

15:27.890 --> 15:29.520
It's cat food.

15:29.520 --> 15:31.090
It's tasty.

15:31.090 --> 15:32.680
Oh!

15:36.530 --> 15:39.400
You're a weird girl.

15:39.400 --> 15:42.370
Say, you should stay here for a while.

15:42.370 --> 15:43.900
What?

15:43.900 --> 15:46.710
Be my friend.

15:46.710 --> 15:48.710
But I...

15:48.710 --> 15:51.550
I'll make sure you have
tasty food to eat every day!

15:51.550 --> 15:54.720
Clothes and purses and jewelry...

15:54.720 --> 15:56.980
I'll buy you whatever you want.

15:56.980 --> 15:59.950
You can get anything as long
as you have money, after all.

15:59.950 --> 16:04.760
So, come on. So, stay with me forever!

16:26.750 --> 16:29.580
What is the meaning of this, villagers?

16:29.580 --> 16:32.620
This is the sacred witch's mansion.

16:32.620 --> 16:34.360
Drop the cheap act!

16:34.360 --> 16:39.430
We already know who you
really are, you damn fake psychic!

16:39.430 --> 16:41.300
How dare you deceive us?!

16:41.300 --> 16:43.760
Return the money we gave you this instant!

16:54.270 --> 16:56.330
Give it back!

16:58.550 --> 17:03.210
Like hell you'd ever understand how I feel.

17:04.180 --> 17:05.880
Whatever!

17:11.790 --> 17:13.620
What the heck is this?!

17:47.330 --> 17:49.490
It's witchcraft!

17:59.340 --> 18:02.430
Ellis, you saved me, didn't you?

18:37.880 --> 18:41.480
This is... your past...

18:41.480 --> 18:44.380
Wait... What is this?

18:44.380 --> 18:46.590
Ellis, don't tell me...

18:46.590 --> 18:48.990
This...

18:48.990 --> 18:51.230
This can't be.

18:51.230 --> 18:52.950
Are you all right?!

19:03.100 --> 19:04.910
Take care, you two.

19:04.910 --> 19:06.410
Same to you.

19:06.410 --> 19:09.980
Make sure you apologize
to everyone in the village.

19:09.980 --> 19:12.470
Well, then, let's meet again later, okay?

19:16.680 --> 19:19.420
Be careful!

19:19.420 --> 19:21.080
All right.

19:29.130 --> 19:31.600
Hello? Is this the White House?

19:31.600 --> 19:35.270
I don't care who, so could you
transfer me to someone really high up?

19:35.270 --> 19:39.210
I've got some incredible information!

19:40.340 --> 19:42.040
Yes, that's right.

19:42.040 --> 19:45.850
An incredible secret that
could be of national importance.

19:45.850 --> 19:48.650
What kind of information is this?

19:48.650 --> 19:50.820
There's this girl called Ellis and...

19:50.820 --> 19:54.560
Wait, let's talk business before we get to that.

19:54.560 --> 19:56.290
What do you mean by business?

19:56.290 --> 19:59.060
I want you to prepare a suitable reward.

19:59.060 --> 20:01.990
Then I'll set up a meeting
for you with Ellis herself.

20:04.870 --> 20:07.370
And I've got one more condition.

20:07.370 --> 20:10.240
I want your guarantee
that you'll let us all live.

20:10.240 --> 20:14.000
Me, Ellis, and a girl named Nadie. Three of us.

20:15.310 --> 20:16.810
All right.

20:16.810 --> 20:18.970
Then I'll call again later.

20:20.810 --> 20:24.650
Wow, that was nerve-wracking!

20:24.650 --> 20:28.320
But everything will work out now.

20:28.320 --> 20:32.730
I'll be able to live in the mansion
in Beverly Hills like the old days.

20:36.730 --> 20:38.720
Like the old days...

20:47.510 --> 20:48.880
What's wrong?

20:48.880 --> 20:50.870
Nothing.

20:53.410 --> 20:57.680
Then we shall merely observe
for the immediate future,

20:57.680 --> 21:01.050
and wait to see what Rosenberg does.

21:01.050 --> 21:03.280
There are no objections, I trust?

21:12.970 --> 21:16.370
Yes, I will head to the location now.

21:22.040 --> 21:24.210
Come to pick me up?

21:24.210 --> 21:26.910
As if she would.

21:29.380 --> 21:32.380
It is deathly hot over there.

21:34.120 --> 21:37.390
Try to limit your activities,
so they don't prove lethal.

22:10.420 --> 22:13.530
- I wonder if she's okay...
- What?

22:13.530 --> 22:15.520
Nothing.

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Like flowers that never die

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
A night of red stars

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
The vanishing warmth

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
I want to keep it here

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
You, with your eyes closed

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Yearning over and over

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
...everything
